ppu_fs: the "[fs] open" line only with PS3_FSLOG, like the other per-call file traces.

cellFsOpen printed every successful open. Resistance 3 opens sound banks, level chunks and streamed data throughout
play, so the log fills with "[fs] open '/dev_hdd0/.../resident_sound.dat' -> fd 68" lines. stat, opendir and mkdir
already print only with PS3_FSLOG; open now does too. Failed opens and FS_CALLER output are unchanged. The switch is
looked up with ps3_env_once, like the file's other PS3_FSLOG checks since #515 (v0.19.0).

Test: tools/test_ppu_fs_open_log.py (runtime/ppu/tests/test_fs_open_log.cpp) runs a successful and a failed open under
no switch, PS3_FSLOG and FS_CALLER and reads stderr; a scripted run (boot, Continue, gameplay) shows no "[fs] open"
lines without PS3_FSLOG and the same lines as before with it.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

